# List comprehension offers a shorter syntax when you want to create
# a new list based on the values of an existing list.
#
# Example:
# Based on a list of fruits, you want a new list containing only the
# fruits with the letter "a" in the name.

# Without list comprehension, you would write a for loop with a
# conditional test inside:

fruits = ["apple", "banana", "cherry", "kiwi", "mango"]

newlist = [x for x in fruits if "a" in x]

print(newlist)
#['apple', 'banana', 'mango']

